Z||000021||CoolBlue87GT||12-14-2001||02:45 PM||||My first reaction to the post was ;<BR> <BR>WHO THE PUCK CARES ??<P>After reading the other responses, I'm able to tone done my response a bit.<P>I'm white, grew up in MD, close to Washington DC, grew up in early 60's.<P>We had many different races in our town / city.  The way things used to be is in my opinion is one worst memories I have of growing up. - (by that, I mean the way people used to treat other races)<P>My Dad was a police officer, and Mom was a school teacher. <P>They brought me up in a way that helped me look at another person and see another person. B/W , another religion, so what.<P>We weren't any better than another race.<P>Since moving to Florida, I've noticed many here are still "back in the 60's" in the way they act toward other races.<P>I've had coworkers try to tell me a racial joke, I'd stop them right there and then, tell them I do not share your views on the subject.<P>I'd continue, and say if you bring this up again in front of me, you will be picking yourself off the floor after I beat the $hit out of them.<P>I've gone up against many people that were a lot bigger then me over this subject. If they brought up that nasty "n" word I'd go ballistic on them.<P>I hate that word, and it show's how ignorant the person saying it is.<P>Now, back to today's post: Interracial marriage.<P>Why worry about it ? They are two people - <B> STOP </B>-  That's it, only two people, it's their business, and only their's.<P>If I saw a 'Interracial couple', all I'd notice is, hmm, I've got that same tie, or shoes.<P>They are just people in love, it's not for anyone to judge, Hey did they do the right thing ?<P>So, I guess my first reaction, WHO THE PUCK CARES, was right after all.<P>(not trying to flame anyone with my comments)<p>[This message has been edited by CoolBlue87GT (edited 12-14-2001).]||||reg||6
