Z||000026||Formula88||12-14-2001||04:01 PM||||There are many different types of "mixed" relationships.  <P>Different races, religions, job class, social stature, political affiliation, etc.<P>IMO, any of them are cool.  It's always "easiest" to date someone of the same race, religion, and a similar social position.  Not saying that's best, but easier.  Like a plumber dating a High Fashion Supermodel.  So they may love one another, but they come from different worlds, so it's more difficult for them to relate in that respect.<P>Rich dating poor.  Again, nothing wrong, but you have to be careful that the weathly person doesn't feel they are being used as a "gravy-train" and the poor person doesn't feel like a "charity case."<P>Different religions?  That can be hardest of all.  Usually, if the dating becomes serious, or if marriage is considered, one person will switch to the other's religion.  Not always, but frequently.  Big family issues there.<P>Politics?  If a Republican and a Democrat breed, do you get Libertarians or Whigs?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Some heated arguments are in store for that couple.||||reg||1
